@startuml cloud_bot_infrastructure_v2
title Cloud Bot - Serverless Webhook Infrastructure (Option A)

left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

actor "Telegram user" as user
cloud "Telegram Bot API\nhttps://api.telegram.org" as telegram

package "GCP Cloud Run (Serverless App Host)" {
  node "Stateless Container\n2GB RAM / 2 vCPU (Scale-to-Zero)" as cloud_run {
    component "Flask API\n/webhook POST endpoint\napp.py" as flask_app
    component "RAG retrieval module\ntop-k + context + citations" as retrieval
    component "multilingual-e5-small\nlocal CPU embeddings\n384 dimensions" as embedder
  }
}

package "Managed Cloud Databases (State & Vector)" {
  database "Qdrant Cloud\ncloud_bot_knowledge\nHTTPS + API key" as qdrant_cloud
  database "Managed Valkey / Upstash\nrediss:// + TLS token\nHistory & Quota counter" as valkey_cloud
}

package "LLM Inference Providers" {
  cloud "Gemini Developer API\nfree tier, quota limited\n(Default LLM)" as gemini_api
  cloud "Modal Qwen3 4B FP16 / L4\npaid, scale-to-zero (60s)\n(Optional LLM)" as modal_paid
  cloud "Vertex AI\noptional paid provider" as vertex
}

folder "Knowledge documents\nMarkdown / TXT, read-only" as documents
component "Local Ingestion CLI\nparse, chunk, local embeddings" as ingestion

artifact ".env / GCP Secrets\nTelegram, Qdrant, Valkey, Modal, Gemini\nGit-ignored" as bot_env

' --- Data Flow & Interconnections ---

user --> telegram : 1. Send chat message
telegram --> flask_app : 2. HTTPS POST /webhook (Push)

flask_app --> valkey_cloud : 3. Check quota counter (400 limit) & fetch 4-turn history
flask_app --> retrieval : 4. Execute RAG query pipeline

retrieval --> embedder : 5. Pass text with "query:" prefix
embedder --> qdrant_cloud : 6. Dense vector search (384d top-k)
qdrant_cloud --> retrieval : 7. Return matching text chunks

flask_app --> gemini_api : 8a. HTTPS generateContent (Default Free)
flask_app ..> modal_paid : 8b. HTTPS inference (If Valkey quota OK)
flask_app ..> vertex : 8c. Optional paid fallback

gemini_api --> flask_app : 9. Stream/Return generated response
modal_paid ..> flask_app : 9. Stream/Return generated response

flask_app --> valkey_cloud : 10. Update chat history & increment quota counter
flask_app --> telegram : 11. HTTPS sendMessage response (200 OK)
telegram --> user : 12. Deliver message to user

documents --> ingestion
ingestion --> embedder : Embed with "passage:" prefix
ingestion --> qdrant_cloud : Upsert vector chunks & metadata

' --- Explanatory Notes ---

note bottom of cloud_run
  **Cloud Run Specs:**
  - Scale-to-Zero when idle ($0 cost)
  - Memory: 2 GiB (Safe for PyTorch/multilingual-e5)
  - CPU: 2 vCPU
  - Free Tier: 2M requests/mo + 180k vCPU-secs
end note

note bottom of modal_paid
  **Modal L4 Configuration:**
  - min_containers=0, max_containers=1
  - 60s idle scale-down
  - SGLang optimized (sm_89)
  - App Quota: Max 400 calls/month (UTC) via Valkey
end note

note bottom of valkey_cloud
  **Managed Valkey State:**
  - Stores 4-turn conversation context
  - Tracks monthly UTC call counter for Modal
  - TLS encrypted connection (rediss://)
end note

@enduml